message: "If you use ViennaFit in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "ViennaFit"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Kostal"
    given-names: "Roman"
    affiliation: "Institute for Microelectronics, TU Wien"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ViennaTools/ViennaFit"
url: "https://viennatools.github.io/ViennaFit/"
license: GPL-3.0-only
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-06-12
keywords:
  - process-simulation
  - parameter-optimization
  - model-calibration
  - sensitivity-analysis
  - semiconductor
abstract: >-
  ViennaFit is a Python package for parameter optimization and calibration
  of ViennaPS process simulation models. It automates the fitting of
  simulation parameters to match experimental data through various
  optimization algorithms and distance metrics, and provides local and
  global sensitivity analysis.
